config FREETZ_PACKAGE_AMUTORRENT
        depends on FREETZ_USER_LEVEL_DEVELOPER
        depends on FREETZ_TARGET_GCC_13_MIN
        depends on FREETZ_OPENSSL_VERSION_30 || FREETZ_OPENSSL_VERSION_35
        bool "aMUTorrent 3.5.0 - DEVELOPER"
        default n
        help
                Experimental package, needs Node.js: installs aMUTorrent as a service
                with full Node.js, with the frontend built on the host system and the
                Express/WebSocket backend running on the target.

                The bootstrap preconfigures a local rTorrent via SCGI directly to
                127.0.0.1:${RTORRENT_SCGI_PORT:-16891} when available.

                The page http://fritz.box:81/amutorrent/ redirects to the service port
                (4000 by default) and displays a diagnostic page if the daemon is not running.

                Note: the Node.js porting on the target is not yet considered functional;
                for this reason the package remains in developer mode, disabled by default,
                and should not be considered ready for normal use.

